{"type":"message","id":"a2e7bc11","parentId":"35333497","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:14:11.795Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"We have `gh` installed; use it read-only. Fetch https://github.com/irae/mendel/issues/13. Your job is to complete that issue: replace eight npm dependencies with native Node equivalents: uuid, xtend, urlsafe-base64, rimraf, glob, chalk, tmp, shasum. Follow the workflow below exactly, in order. Do not read all the code — read only the files your greps point you to.\n\nWords used below: a \"dependency\" is one of the eight npm packages you are removing. A \"package\" is a workspace package of this repo (under packages/, examples/, legacy-packages/, or the repo root). A \"file\" is one source file that uses a dependency.\n\nAs AGENTS.md says, `legacy-packages/` are frozen legacy: change their files when needed, but write no tests and run no tests there.\n\nDirection for chalk: replace it with `util.styleText` and keep Node's defaults. Do not force color on or off — drop the `enableColor` option and the forced color level; that small feature goes away.\n\nSETUP\n\n- Create TASKS.md at the repo root (it is already git-ignored): one `- [ ]` item per dependency, in the issue's order, no sub-items yet.\n\nPER DEPENDENCY — repeat for each of the eight, one at a time\n\n1. Find every use first:\n   a. Grep the whole repo for `require('<dep>')` and every package.json for `\"<dep>\":`.\n   b. In TASKS.md, add one `- [ ]` sub-item per affected file, grouped by package.\n   c. Trust your grep over the issue's list — the issue misses references.\n2. Rewrite one file at a time:\n   a. If the file has no test covering it: first write a small test that passes WITH the dependency still in place. After your change, the same test must pass WITHOUT it.\n   b. Edit only what the grep found. Minimal diff, match neighboring style, no drive-by cleanups.\n   c. Run the owning package's tests (for example `npx tap packages/<pkg>/test/*.js`). Fix what broke.\n   d. Mark the file's sub-item done in TASKS.md.\n3. Drop the dependency with pnpm — never by hand-editing package.json or the lockfile: `pnpm --filter <pkg> remove <dep>` for each package that declares it, `pnpm remove -w <dep>` if the repo root declares it. Pipe through `tail -5`.\n4. Commit everything the dependency touched, in one or more commits, split per package — each commit carries one package's changes with its share of the lockfile update. The root package.json change may ride with one package's commit or come as its own commit; both are fine. Before every commit, run the full unit suite (`pnpm run unit`, pipe through `tail`).\n5. Check the per-dependency acceptance criteria below. Only when all pass, mark the dependency done in TASKS.md and move to the next one.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA — per dependency, before it is marked done\n\n- [ ] Re-grep `require('<dep>')`: zero uses left in code. Test fixture data under `test/fixtures/` is parser input, not a use.\n- [ ] Re-grep `\"<dep>\":`: no package.json anywhere still declares it — legacy-packages and root included.\n- [ ] `pnpm-lock.yaml` shrank; every removal went through `pnpm remove`.\n- [ ] All changes committed — root package.json included — type `chore`, split per package, exact file paths staged (never `git add -A`), never `--no-verify`.\n- [ ] The full unit suite ran before every commit.\n- [ ] Every sub-item of the dependency is checked in TASKS.md.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA — global, after the eighth dependency\n\n- [ ] Run `npx prettier --check .` and `npx eslint .` yourself; both silent after you fix what they flag.\n- [ ] Run the full suite one last time; it matches the baseline failures listed below.\n- [ ] Every TASKS.md item is checked.\n\nKNOWN PITFALLS — each has caused real failures\n\n- rimraf silently no-ops on a missing path. `fs.rmSync` throws unless you pass `{recursive: true, force: true}` — always pass `force: true` where rimraf was used.\n- Pre-existing failures that are NOT yours to fix (they fail the same way before your change): `legacy-packages/**`. Don't run legacy tests at all\n"}],"timestamp":1788675251795}}
